  "doc": "d8-weapons: Rivet's held weapons drawn for a raised camera (HeldPitchArt). Keyed by the view row's camera pitch in whole degrees (\"55\" = `tilt`; a \"70\" block can sit beside it), then by weapon_art id: art = a three-quarter part showing the gun's top and its side body, +x along the barrel (mirrored about the barrel line while it points left on screen), grip_px = where the gun claw closes, muzzle_px = the bore tip (the flash and the shot start here), length_px = the tail-to-tip span, drawn weapon_art's length_m long. A weapon without a row keeps weapon_art's top-down part; `top` (90) never reads this table. `--held-pitch=off` = the before.",
